  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* working precision. The deep states ([5,4,3], [4,4,4]: ‖Ψ‖ ~ ε^-10, ε^-12) lose many digits to the x0 normalization and to the cancellations in top-killing and cleaning, so 120 digits are not enough at ε ≤ 10^-5. Work at 250, fit clean spaces at εfit = 10^-6, and drop everything memoized at the setup precision *)\npr = 250; εfit = 10^-6;\nScan[(DownValues[#] = Select[DownValues[#], ! FreeQ[#, Pattern] &]) &, {EN, Etot, lax2, tL2}];\nGrid[{{\"working precision\", pr}, {\"ε for fitting clean spaces\", εfit}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
