   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results (2026-10-02, P1, 250 digits)\n- **Same order.** For every HW state of $[4,2,0]^2$, each insertion's top-killed contamination has the same $\\varepsilon$-order as its signal, or a higher one. So **leading-order cleaning suffices**; no deep cancellation is needed. This includes $[5,4,3]$ ($\\|\\Psi\\|\\sim\\varepsilon^{-10}$) and $[4,4,4]$ ($\\varepsilon^{-12}$).\n- **Structural.** The contamination ratios are $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent up to $O(\\varepsilon)$: the spread is $1.4\\times10^{-3}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$ and $1.4\\times10^{-4}$ at $10^{-6}$. The coefficient is larger than for $[3,1,0]$.\n- **Clean spaces.** Fitted per sector at $(\\varepsilon=10^{-6},\\varphi,\\omega)$. Restricted to $\\mathrm{HW}_\\mu$ over five $w$, they have full rank for **every** sector except $[6,4,2]$:\n  - rank 2 on $[7,4,1]$, $[7,3,2]$, $[6,5,1]$ and **$[5,4,3]$**;\n  - rank 1 on the multiplicity-1 sectors, including **$[4,4,4]$**.\n- **$[6,4,2]$ (multiplicity 3).** The three copies' contamination vectors span only 2 dimensions, and the common clean space reaches rank 2 at leading order (the third singular value is $\\propto\\varepsilon$). The raw insertions do have rank 3 on it. **Per-copy** clean spaces, which need only the copy's own constraint, work.\n- **End to end.** The input is the Q-side numbers $(X^B-W_X\\cdot e_1e_1)\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ only, with $X^B$ computed by acting on $\\Psi$. The clean combinations were fitted at $(\\varepsilon=10^{-6},\\varphi)$ and then applied at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$, and at $\\varepsilon=10^{-4},10^{-5}$ with a different $\\varphi'$. Least squares then recovers $P_{\\rm HW}\\Psi$, **scale included, for all 18 non-top HW states**. Relative errors are $\\sim10^{-4}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-4}$ and $\\sim10^{-5}$ at $10^{-5}$, i.e. $O(\\varepsilon)$, with $\\ge115$ correct digits. Sector-wide cleaning is used everywhere except $[6,4,2]$, which uses per-copy cleaning.\n- **So:** the seven localized insertions plus $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ determine **all** CG data of $[4,2,0]^2$, including $[5,4,3]$ and $[4,4,4]$, through clean leading-order combinations. The earlier \"blind spot\" is gone. Also, 120 digits were not enough for $[4,4,4]$ at $\\varepsilon\\le10^{-5}$: they gave zero-accuracy \"exact\" errors.\n- **Caveats.**\n  - The clean coefficients are fitted from the states' own contamination vectors. They are structural, but not in closed form.\n  - $[6,4,2]$ needs copy-specific coefficients.\n  - One chain point only.\n  - The eigenvalues stand in for Q's.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Site 1 only\nHow crucial are the site-2 insertions? Repeat Section 2 using only the four site-1 insertions ($T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,2)},T_{(3,2)},T_{(4,2)}$ at $\\theta_1-4h$) plus $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$, which is used for top-killing. For each sector the table gives:\n- the sector-wide clean space and its HW rank;\n- the per-copy clean spaces and their HW ranks;\n- the fair end-to-end error: fitted at $(\\varepsilon_{\\rm fit},\\varphi)$, tested at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$ with $\\varphi'$. It uses the sector-wide space where that has full rank, and per-copy spaces otherwise.\n\nA relative singular value that shrinks with $\\varepsilon$ means that direction is lost at leading order.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "embed[v_, sub_] := ReplacePart[ConstantArray[0, 7], Thread[sub -> v]];\ncleanSub[μ_, sub_] := cleanSub[μ, sub] = Module[{rows = Table[KSn[μ, c, εfit, φ, ω][\"k\"][[sub]], {c, Length[hwB[μ]]}], sv, r, V},\n   sv = SingularValueList[rows, Tolerance -> 0]; r = Count[sv, x_ /; x > 10^-3 Max[sv]];\n   V = SingularValueDecomposition[rows][[3]]; embed[#, sub] & /@ Transpose[V][[r + 1 ;;]]];\ncleanOneSub[μ_, c_, sub_] := cleanOneSub[μ, c, sub] = With[{k = KSn[μ, c, εfit, φ, ω][\"k\"][[sub]]}, embed[#, sub] & /@ NullSpace[{k/Norm[k]}, Tolerance -> 10^-6]];\nsite1 = {1, 2, 3, 4};\nfullRankQ[sv_, m_] := Length[sv] >= m && sv[[m]] > 10^-3;\n{tS1, s1Tab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[Module[{mult = Length[hwB[μ]], cs, rk4, rk5, pc, use},\n     cs = cleanSub[μ, site1];\n     rk4 = If[cs === {}, {}, Take[hwRank[μ, cs, 10^-4], UpTo[mult + 1]]]; rk5 = If[cs === {}, {}, Take[hwRank[μ, cs, 10^-5], UpTo[mult + 1]]];\n     pc = Table[With[{c1 = cleanOneSub[μ, c, site1]}, Take[hwRank[μ, c1, 10^-5], UpTo[mult + 1]]], {c, mult}];\n     {μ, mult, Length[cs], rk4, rk5, pc,\n      Table[With[{vs = If[fullRankQ[rk5, mult] && fullRankQ[rk4, mult], cs, cleanOneSub[μ, c, site1]]}, With[{r = reconHW[μ, c, 10^-5, vs, φp]}, {If[vs === cs, \"sector\", \"per copy\"], r[[1]], r[[3]]}]], {c, mult}]}], {μ, Rest[hwSecs]}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"mult\", \"dim sector clean (site 1)\", \"sector HW rel. sv, ε=10^-4\", \"ε=10^-5\", \"per-copy HW rel. sv (ε=10^-5)\", \"end to end per copy: {space, rel. err (ε=10^-5, φ'), digits}\"}}, s1Tab, {{\"time (s)\", tS1, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"942214\" data-output-id=\"52\" data-out-n=\"555\" data-sub-idx=\"6\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"13\" data-sub-start=\"13\" data-sub-end=\"13\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[555]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"26\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:24.1101em;vertical-align:-11.7851em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.3251em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.2851em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:14.2851em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:24.0701em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-11.7851em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.2851em;\"><span style=\"top:-15.4951em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-14.2851em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">8</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mo