   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Observation.** With $t=\\theta_{12}/h$ ($t-1=27/35$):\n- $\\tilde k^{[8,2,2]}=(t-1)\\,(0,0,-1,1)=(t-1)\\,\\tilde s^{[8,3,1]}$;\n- $\\tilde k^{[6,6,0]}=(t-1)\\,(1,2,-2,1)=(t-1)\\,\\tilde s^{[7,5,0]}$;\n- $\\tilde k=0$ for $[8,3,1]$ and $[7,5,0]$, whose only neighbour above is the top $[8,4,0]$, already killed exactly.\n\n**Hypothesis.** The leading contamination of a HW state of weight $\\mu$ lies in the span of the **signals of the HW states one root above**, i.e. the sectors $\\mu+\\alpha_1$, $\\mu+\\alpha_2$, $\\mu+\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$. Here $\\alpha_1=(1,-1,0)$, $\\alpha_2=(0,1,-1)$, and the top sector is excluded because it is killed. The test uses all seven insertions (7-vectors), at $\\varepsilon=10^{-6}$ and $2\\times10^{-6}$. It reports the relative residual of projecting $K^B$ onto the span of the neighbours' $S^{B'}$, for simple-root neighbours only and with $\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$ included. If the hypothesis is right, the residual is $O(\\varepsilon)$, halving from $2\\times10^{-6}$ to $10^{-6}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result of the one-step test.**\n- **[8,2,2] and [6,6,0]:** the contamination lies in the span of the simple-root neighbour's signal, with residual $\\sim10^{-7}$ scaling as $O(\\varepsilon)$.\n- **[7,3,2] and [6,5,1]:** the same holds once the $\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$ neighbour is included, with residual $10^{-7}$–$10^{-9}$.\n- **[6,4,2]:** the residual is small, but with 6 neighbour vectors in 7 dimensions the test is weak.\n- **[7,4,1]:** its contamination is already subleading.\n- **The deeper states [6,3,3], [5,5,2], [5,4,3] and [4,4,4] fail** (residual $O(1)$).\n\n**Sharper test.** The expansion coefficients must not depend on $w$, so stack $K^B$ and the neighbours' $S^{B'}$ over the five $w$ (35-component vectors). Then test $K^B\\in\\mathrm{span}\\{S^{B'}\\}$, where $B'$ runs over (i) the one-step neighbours and (ii) all HW states strictly above $\\mu$ in the dominance order ($\\nu-\\mu=a\\alpha_1+b\\alpha_2$ with $a,b\\ge0$), top excluded. If (ii) holds, the leading contamination is a $w$-independent combination of higher irreps' signals.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "stackK[μc_, ε_] := Flatten[Table[KSn[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], ε, φ, ωv][\"K\"], {ωv, ωSet}]];\nstackS[μc_, ε_] := Flatten[Table[KSn[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], ε, φ, ωv][\"S\"], {ωv, ωSet}]];\nabove[μ_] := Select[nonTop, #[[1]] =!= μ && #[[1, 1]] >= μ[[1]] && #[[1, 3]] <= μ[[3]] &];\n{t6c, hyp2} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[Module[{res},\n     res = Table[With[{k = stackK[μc, ε], s = stackS[μc, ε]}, {Norm[k]/Norm[s], projRes[k, stackS[#, ε] & /@ neighbours[μc[[1]], {α1, α2, α1 + α2}]], projRes[k, stackS[#, ε] & /@ above[μc[[1]]]]}], {ε, {10^-6, 2 10^-6}}];\n     {μc[[1]], μc[[2]], Length[above[μc[[1]]]], N[res[[1, 1]], 2], N[res[[1, 2]], 2], N[res[[1, 3]], 2], N[res[[2, 3]], 2]}], {μc, nonTop}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"# HW states above\", \"‖K‖/‖S‖ (stacked)\", \"residual vs one-step nbrs\", \"residual vs all above, ε=10^-6\", \"2×10^-6\"}}, hyp2, {{\"time (s)\", t6c, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
