  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results of Section 6 (2026-10-02, P1, $t=\\theta_{12}/h=62/35$)\n**1. Top-killing.** The top-killed Q-number is $(X^B-X^{\\rm top})\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$, where $X^{\\rm top}$ is the eigenvalue on $e_1\\otimes e_1$.\n\n**2. Signal ratios are simple rationals.** In the basis $X_\\lambda=T_\\lambda/f_\\lambda$, $\\lambda=(1,1),(2,2),(3,2),(4,2)$, normalized to $(4,2)$, the leading $\\tilde s$ are:\n\n| $\\mu$ | $\\tilde s$ |\n|---|---|\n| [8,3,1] | $(0,0,-1,1)$ |\n| [8,2,2] | $(0,0,0,1)$ |\n| [7,5,0] | $(1,2,-2,1)$ |\n| [6,6,0] | $(0,2,-2,1)$ |\n| [6,3,3] | $(0,0,-\\tfrac15,1)$ |\n| [5,5,2] | $(0,0,-\\tfrac45,1)$ |\n| [4,4,4] | $(0,0,0,1)$ |\n\n**3. Contamination ratios.**\n- **Zero** for $[8,3,1]$ and $[7,5,0]$. Their only neighbour above is the top, which is killed exactly, so every combination is clean.\n- **$[8,2,2]$:** $\\tilde k=(t-1)\\,\\tilde s^{[8,3,1]}=(t-1)(0,0,-1,1)$. Clean condition: $c_{32}=c_{42}$.\n- **$[6,6,0]$:** $\\tilde k=(t-1)\\,\\tilde s^{[7,5,0]}=(t-1)(1,2,-2,1)$. Clean condition: $c_{11}+2c_{22}-2c_{32}+c_{42}=0$.\n- **Interpretation.** The leading contamination of $\\mu$ is the signal pattern of the irrep one simple root above, times $(t-1)$. The statement holds pointwise in $w$, in this normalized form. The raw coefficient relating $K^B$ to $S^{B'}$ depends on $w$: the stacked-$w$ test fails, because the two signals carry different $w$-monomials.\n- **One-root span test (single $w$, 7 insertions):** holds to $O(\\varepsilon)$ for $[7,3,2]$ and $[6,5,1]$ once $\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$ is included.\n- **Deeper states ($[6,3,3]$, $[5,5,2]$, $[5,4,3]$, $[4,4,4]$):** $\\tilde k$ is not a recognizable rational at P1. For example, $[4,4,4]$ has $\\tilde k\\approx(0.01310,-0.00319,-0.26558,0.13820)$.\n\n**Open.**\n- Deeper states presumably collect contamination from several irreps above, including the multiplicity copies of $[6,4,2]$ and $[7,3,2]$. Their weights would then involve those copies' spectral data, which are algebraic rather than rational (compare the octet $\\kappa$'s $(2\\pm\\sqrt{4+5t^2})/t^2$ for $[2,1,0]$). Test this by expanding $\\tilde k^{\\mu}$ in the $\\tilde s^{\\nu}$ of all states above, with extra insertions (e.g. non-localized $t(u)$) so the span test is not trivially satisfied.\n- Then rewrite the clean conditions in the single-Q variables.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "α1 = {1, -1, 0}; α2 = {0, 1, -1};\nprojRes[k_, vs_] := If[vs === {}, If[Norm[k] == 0, 0, 1], With[{B = Orthogonalize[vs]}, Norm[k - (B . k) . B]/Norm[k]]];\nneighbours[μ_, roots_] := Select[nonTop, MemberQ[μ + # & /@ roots, #[[1]]] &];\nhypTest[μc_, ε_] := Module[{d = KSn[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], ε, φ, ω], nb1, nb2},\n   nb1 = neighbours[μc[[1]], {α1, α2}]; nb2 = neighbours[μc[[1]], {α1, α2, α1 + α2}];\n   {Norm[d[\"K\"]]/Norm[d[\"S\"]], projRes[d[\"K\"], Table[KSn[b[[1]], b[[2]], ε, φ, ω][\"S\"], {b, nb1}]], projRes[d[\"K\"], Table[KSn[b[[1]], b[[2]], ε, φ, ω][\"S\"], {b, nb2}]], Length[nb1], Length[nb2]}];\n{t6b, hyp} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{a = hypTest[μc, 10^-6], b = hypTest[μc, 2 10^-6]}, {μc[[1]], μc[[2]], a[[4]], a[[5]], N[a[[1]], 3], N[a[[2]], 3], N[b[[2]], 3], N[a[[3]], 3], N[b[[3]], 3]}], {μc, nonTop}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"# simple-root nbrs\", \"# incl. α1+α2\", \"‖K‖/‖S‖\", \"residual vs simple-root nbrs, ε=10^-6\", \"2×10^-6\", \"residual incl. α1+α2, ε=10^-6\", \"2×10^-6\"}}, hyp, {{\"time (s)\", t6b, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
